{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZbJn4q5F5R65pZwnRxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture of the codebase. Let me summarize my analysis findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController` at line 20-56 in `ShipmentController.kt` handles shipment endpoints\n- `Shipment` data class at line 9-14 with `ShipmentStatus` enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED) at line 23-27\n- `InMemoryShipmentRepository` provides `save()` and `findById()` methods\n- Error handling pattern: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409) in `ApiExceptions.kt`\n- `ErrorCode` enum in `ApiError.kt` defines error codes (currently: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers use `@PostMapping`, `@GetMapping`, `@PathVariable` annotations\n- Errors are thrown as sealed `ApiException` subclasses\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with assertions on status codes and JSON paths using `jsonPath()`\n- Response status uses `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus)` for non-200 responses\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add the new confirm endpoint\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for the new endpoint\n3. `ApiError.kt` - Need to add a new ErrorCode for when a shipment cannot be confirmed (CANCELLED state)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Not handling idempotent behavior (same request twice should succeed)\n- Not properly distinguishing between different error conditions (CANCELLED vs NOT_FOUND)\n- Breaking existing tests\n\n**Open questions:** None - the requirements are clear on the HTTP status codes and behavior for all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to handle attempts to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   This method will:\n   - Check if shipment exists; throw `ResourceNotFoundException` if not (404)\n   - If shipment is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with the new error code (409)\n   - If shipment is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED, persist it, and return it\n   - If shipment is already CONFIRMED, return it unchanged (idempotent, no error)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with appropriate error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using HTTP 200 for CANCELLED case instead of 409: Rejected because the requirement explicitly states 409, which correctly indicates a conflict with the current state rather than a server error or success.\n- Not adding a new error code and reusing an existing one: Rejected because existing error codes (e.g., SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS) don't semantically match the \"cannot confirm because cancelled\" scenario.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | `findById()` returns CREATED shipment | `save()` with CONFIRMED status | 200 OK, shipment object | Success case |\n| Already CONFIRMED | `findById()` returns CONFIRMED shipment | No write | 200 OK, unchanged shipment object | Idempotent success |\n| CANCELLED | `findById()` returns CANCELLED shipment | No write | 409 Conflict, error envelope with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED | ConflictException |\n| Not found | `findById()` returns null | No write | 404 Not Found, error envelope with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test \"confirms a CREATED shipment\"**: Create S-1, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n2. **Test \"idempotent confirm already CONFIRMED shipment\"**: Create and confirm S-2, confirm again, verify still CONFIRMED with 200 OK\n3. **Test \"rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment\"**: Manually save a CANCELLED shipment S-3, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED error code\n4. **Test \"rejects confirming a non-existent shipment\"**: Attempt confirm on S-missing, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1338,"cache_read_input_tokens":18296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1338},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"160d4e53-d914-4f06-918a-a9ec2d220f91","uuid":"2757645e-4069-492e-b29c-7c5f945a81d6","timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:04:31.862Z","request_id":"req_011CfZbJmiVjhE2qjfGrLweL"}
